# Class: <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000967> (temperature)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000967> "The concept refers to an absolute temperature, not to be mistaken with temperature difference."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000967> "To express that an object has a temperature, the property 'intensive bearer of' can be used. It implies a chain of: object consists of some portion of matter and portion of matter bearer of some temperature."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000967> "temperature"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000967> "The temperature is a fundamental intensive quality representing the average atomic or molcular movement or vibration of a portion of matter."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000060> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000967> "true"^^xsd:boolean)
SubClassOf(<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000967> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020131>)

# Class: <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020003> (crystal)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020003> "crystal"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020003> "A crystal is an object that has a quality \"crystal structure\"."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000060> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020003> "true"^^xsd:boolean)
SubClassOf(<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020003> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000030>)
SubClassOf(<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020003> ObjectSomeValuesFrom(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0000086> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000591>))

# Class: <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020005> (porosity)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020005> "porosity"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020005> "itensive quality embodiying the fraction of the materials (enclosing) spatial region occupied by pores."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000060> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020005> "true"^^xsd:boolean)
SubClassOf(<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020005> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020131>)

# Class: <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020023> (metallic grain structures)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020023> "metallic grain structures"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020023> "The metallic grain structures is a categorical value specification that specifies value of the  metallic grain structure quality. It describes the morphology of polycrystalline metallic materials. Polycrystalline metallic materials will typically form their grain structures as one of those categories or a transition or mixture state of those."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000060> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020023> "true"^^xsd:boolean)
EquivalentClasses(<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020023> ObjectOneOf(<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020027> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020097> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020100> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020107> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020109> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020110> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020111>))
SubClassOf(<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020023> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OBI_0001930>)

# Class: <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020099> (bravais lattice (3D))

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020099> "TODO: possibly extend for 2D (Graphene etc)

More elaborate crystal descriptions may be found in http://emmo.info/domain-crystallography/crystallography or https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/disos/cso"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020099> "bravais lattice (3D)"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020099> "The bravais lattice is a categorical value specification that specifies value of the crystal structure quality. It describes the possible geometric arrangement of lattice points in a crystal. The present descriptor is limited to the 14 possible three-dimensional arrangements."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000060> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020099> "true"^^xsd:boolean)
EquivalentClasses(<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020099> ObjectOneOf(<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020006> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020007> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020008> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020009> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020010> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020011> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020012> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020013> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020014> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020015> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020016> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020017> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020018> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020019>))
SubClassOf(<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020099> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OBI_0001930>)

# Class: <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020106> (polycrystal)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020106> "polycrystal"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020106> "Polycrystalline structure"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020106> "A polycrystal is a connected material entity aggregate that consists of multiple crystal grains joined through crystallographic interfaces."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000060> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020106> "true"^^xsd:boolean)
SubClassOf(<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020106> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000890>)
SubClassOf(<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020106> ObjectSomeValuesFrom(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000051> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000663>))

# Class: <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020112> (grain size distribution)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020112> "grain size distribution"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020112> "An intensive quality describing the lower length scale object aggregate (grains) that is part of the material."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000060> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020112> "true"^^xsd:boolean)
SubClassOf(<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020112> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020131>)

# Class: <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020116> (aggregate state value)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020116> "aggregate state value"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020116> "The aggregate state value is a categorical value specification that specifies value of the aggregate state quality."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000060> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020116> "true"^^xsd:boolean)
EquivalentClasses(<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020116> ObjectOneOf(<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020117> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020118> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020119> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020120> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020121> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020122> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020123> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020124> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020125>))
SubClassOf(<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020116> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OBI_0001930>)

# Class: <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020131> (intensive quality)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020131> "intensive quality"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020131> "Point property"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020131> "An intensive quality is a quality that inheres in only portion of matter and thus is independent of the bearers (system-) size."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000060> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020131> "true"^^xsd:boolean)
SubClassOf(<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020131> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000019>)
SubClassOf(Annotation(rdfs:comment "Due to the duality of object and portion of matter this axiom can not be an equivalent class axiom."@en) <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020131> ObjectSomeValuesFrom(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0000080> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000001>))
DisjointClasses(<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020131> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020148>)

# Class: <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020148> (extensive quality)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020148> "extensive quality"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020148> "An extensive quality is a quality that inheres in only object or object aggregate or fiat object part or chemical entity and is dependent on the bearers (system-) size."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000060> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020148> "true"^^xsd:boolean)
SubClassOf(<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020148> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000019>)

# Class: <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020197> (lattice point)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020197> "lattice point"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020197> "A lattice point is a fiat point that represents a position in a crystal lattice at which structural entities are regularly arranged."@en)
SubClassOf(<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020197> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000147>)
SubClassOf(<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020197> ObjectSomeValuesFrom(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000050> <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000001>))
SubClassOf(<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020197> ObjectSomeValuesFrom(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0001015> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_33250>))

# Class: <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020216> (order scale value)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020216> "order scale value"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020216> "possible values of characteristic length over which structural correlations persist in a material"@en)
EquivalentClasses(<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020216> ObjectOneOf(<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020217> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020218> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020219> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020242>))
SubClassOf(<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020216> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OBI_0001930>)

# Class: <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020220> (order scale)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020220> "order scale"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020220> "characteristic length over which structural correlations persist in a material"@en)
EquivalentClasses(<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020220> ObjectExactCardinality(1 <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000077> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020216>))
SubClassOf(<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020220> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020131>)
SubClassOf(<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020220> ObjectSomeValuesFrom(<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000077> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020216>))

# Class: <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020243> (grain size)

AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000116> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020243> "size values of indiviudal grains are properties of the respective objects"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020243> "grain size"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020243> "an intensive quality epitomizing the average size of the grains of a polycrystal"@en)
SubClassOf(<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020243> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020131>)
SubClassOf(<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020243> ObjectSomeValuesFrom(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0000080> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020106>))

# Class: <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0025001> (composition)

AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000116> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0025001> "There's a dfference between composition and chemical compositon for the following reason: chemical compositon is relevant when the mass/volume/mole proportions of chemical elements(!) are identified, whlist composition includes proportions of molecules, other pure chemical substances, or even proptions of objects (in an object aggregate)."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0025001> "composition"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0025001> "Composition is an intensive quality which defines types and proportions of compounds present in a material entity and is subject of some composition data item."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0025001> "4 vol.% nitric acid solution, Styrene-Butadiene-Styrene (SBS) Block Copolymer with 50 vol.% of both styrene and butadiene"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000060> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0025001> "true"^^xsd:boolean)
AnnotationAssertion(<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000064> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0025001> "Composition is a collective property of a portion of matter, i.e., the triple portion of matter has quality composition holds. As \"has quality\" is an inverse  functional property, only one instance of portion of matter can have this specific composition. However, proportions describe the relation between the prortion of matter (the whole) and some compound (the part). Thus, the following triples hold: portion of matter has relational quality proportion; portion of matter has part some substance (or whatever is your part); substance has relational quality proportion. \"Has relational quality\" is not inverse functional, i.e., it can point to a single object from 2 distinct subjects."@en)
SubClassOf(<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0025001> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020131>)

# Class: <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0025003> (metallic grain structure)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0025003> "ferrite, austenite, martensite, etc."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0025003> "metallic grain structure"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0025003> "intensive quality epitomizing the distinct phases in the microscopic structure of a metallic material."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000060> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0025003> "false"^^xsd:boolean)
EquivalentClasses(<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0025003> ObjectExactCardinality(1 <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000077> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020023>))
SubClassOf(<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0025003> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020131>)
SubClassOf(<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0025003> ObjectSomeValuesFrom(<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000077> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020023>))

# Class: <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000000> (unit cell)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000000> "unit cell"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000000> "Unit cell is a site which is a part of a crystal lattice and represents the smallest volume, from which the lattice can be constructed by translational displacements. Unit cell is characterized by the length of its sides and their angular relations."@en)
SubClassOf(<https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000000> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000029>)

# Class: <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000001> (crystal lattice)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000001> "TODO: 
1. check if located in is meant to be used this way
2. Is there a better alternative to has part?"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000001> "crystal lattice"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000001> "Crystal lattice is a site which has unit cell as part and is location of a crystal. It represents a periodic array of points in space, which describe the arrangement of atoms or molecules in a crystal."@en)
SubClassOf(<https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000001> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000029>)
SubClassOf(<https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000001> ObjectSomeValuesFrom(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000051> <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000000>))
SubClassOf(<https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000001> ObjectSomeValuesFrom(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0001015> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020003>))

# Class: <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000011> (crystallographic plane)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000011> "crystallographic plane"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000011> "Crystallographic plane is a fiat surface which is part of a crystal lattice and which is denoted by Miller indices of a plane."@en)
SubClassOf(<https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000011> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000146>)
SubClassOf(<https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000011> ObjectSomeValuesFrom(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000050> <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000001>))

# Class: <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000012> (crystallographic direction)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000012> "crystallographic direction"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000012> "Crystallographic direction is a fiat line which is part of a crystal lattice and which is denoted by Miller indices of a direction."@en)
SubClassOf(<https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000012> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000142>)
SubClassOf(<https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000012> ObjectSomeValuesFrom(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000050> <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000001>))

# Class: <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000014> (Miller indices)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000014> "TODO 
1. think if its actually 1D..
2. Review the definitions of sublcasses"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000014> "Miller indices"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000014> "Miller indices is an information content entity which denotes crystallographic direction, crystallographic plane, or lattice point, i.e., defines their position in respect to the coordinate system of a crystal lattice, and has exactly 3 interger literals, namely h, k. and l."@en)
SubClassOf(<https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000014> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000501>)
SubClassOf(<https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000014> DataExactCardinality(3 <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000016>))

# Class: <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000020> (direction Miller indices)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000020> "direction Miller indices"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000020> "Direction Miller indices define the components of a sinlge vector in the given direction in a crystal's unit cell. Usually, direction Miller indices are reduced to the lowest set of integers. Direction Miller indices must be written in square brackets, e.g., [hkl]."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000020> "[111]")
SubClassOf(<https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000020> <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000014>)
SubClassOf(<https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000020> ObjectSomeValuesFrom(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000219> <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000012>))

# Class: <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000021> (family of directions Miller indices)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000021> "family of directions Miller indices"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000021> "<111>")
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000021> "Set of directions Miller indices define the components of symmetrically equivalent directions in a crystal lattice. Set of directions Miller indices must be written as <hkl>."@en)
SubClassOf(<https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000021> <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000014>)
SubClassOf(<https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000021> ObjectSomeValuesFrom(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000219> <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000012>))

# Class: <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000022> (plane Miller indices)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000022> "plane Miller indices"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000022> "Plane Miller indices define the reciprocals of the fractional intercepts the plane makes with the crystallographic axes, reduced to the lowest set of integers. 
For example, if a plane crosses [100] axis at 1/h, [010 ] axis at 1/k, and [001] axis at 1/l, then such plane is denoted as (hkl) plane. If a plane is parallel to one of the axes, then the corresponding Miller index is 0.
Plane Miller indices must be written in round brackets, e.g., (hkl)."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000022> "(hkl)")
SubClassOf(<https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000022> <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000014>)
SubClassOf(<https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000022> ObjectSomeValuesFrom(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000219> <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000011>))

# Class: <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000023> (family of planes Miller indices)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000023> "family of planes Miller indices"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000023> "Set of planes Miller indices define set of symmetrically equivalent planes. Set of planes must be written in curly brackets, e.g., {hkl}."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000023> "{111}")
SubClassOf(<https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000023> <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000014>)
SubClassOf(<https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000023> ObjectSomeValuesFrom(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000219> <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000011>))

# Class: <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000024> (point Miller indices)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000024> "point Miller indices"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000024> "Point Miller indices define the coordinates of a point within a unit cell of a crystal. Point Miller indices must be given in round brackets separated by commas, e.g., (h, k, l)."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000024> "(1,1,1)")
SubClassOf(<https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000024> <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000014>)
SubClassOf(<https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000024> ObjectSomeValuesFrom(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000219> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020197>))

# Class: <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000026> (crystal system)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000026> "('quality of' some 'crystal lattice') potentially crystal system is a quality of a crystal lattice. But then we need the connection between crystal lattice, grains, etc. and its complicated")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000026> "defintion from Introduction to Textur Analysis. TODO: add proper annnotation property"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000026> "crystal system"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000026> "lattice type"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000026> "Crystal system is a intensive quality of a crystal lattice which describes the arrangement of lattice points in an infinite 3D space in such way that each lattice point has an identical environment to that around every other lattice point. It is specified by one of the 7 crystaa sytem value."@en)
SubClassOf(<https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000026> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000019>)
SubClassOf(<https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000026> ObjectSomeValuesFrom(<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000077> <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000028>))
SubClassOf(<https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000026> ObjectExactCardinality(1 <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000077> <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000028>))

# Class: <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000027> (lattice centering)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000027> "lattice centering"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000027> "Lattice centering is an intensive quality ofa crystal lattice which the geometric arrangement of lattice points in a unit cell. It is specified by one of the 4 lattice centering value."@en)
SubClassOf(<https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000027> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000019>)
SubClassOf(<https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000027> ObjectIntersectionOf(ObjectSomeValuesFrom(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0000080> <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000001>) ObjectExactCardinality(1 <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000077> <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000036>)))
SubClassOf(<https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000027> ObjectSomeValuesFrom(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0000080> <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000001>))
SubClassOf(<https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000027> ObjectSomeValuesFrom(<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000077> <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000036>))

# Class: <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000028> (crystal system value)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000028> "crystal system value"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000028> "crystal system value is a categorical value specification which describes the grouping of
crystal structures according to the axial system used to describe their lattice It is a set of three axes in a particular geometrical arrangement: triclinic, monoclinic, orthorhombic, tetragonal, rhombohedral (trigonal), hexagonal, and cubic (isometric)."@en)
EquivalentClasses(<https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000028> ObjectOneOf(<https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000029> <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000030> <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000031> <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000032> <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000033> <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000034> <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000035>))
SubClassOf(<https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000028> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OBI_0001930>)
SubClassOf(<https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000028> ObjectHasSelf(<https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000053>))

# Class: <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000036> (lattice centering value)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000036> "lattice centering value"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000036> "Lattice centering value is a categorical value specification which describes th geometric arrangement of lattice points in a unit cell with one of the values: primitive, body centered, face centered, base centered."@en)
EquivalentClasses(<https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000036> ObjectOneOf(<https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000043> <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000044> <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000045> <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000046>))
SubClassOf(<https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000036> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OBI_0001930>)

# Class: <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000041> (crystallographic entity in cubic system)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000041> "'immaterial entity' and ('part of' some 
('crystal lattice' and ('has quality' some 
('crystal system' and ('specified by value' value cubic)))))")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000041> "crystallographic entity in cubic system"@en)
